\vspace{1.5em}

Dear Hiring Team,

\vspace{0.8em}

I am a Data Science graduate from the University of Maryland and spent a year as a Machine Learning Intern at Nokia, where I built retrieval infrastructure for large-scale RAG systems. My primary project involved building a Knowledge Layer that unified vector search (OpenSearch), relational metadata (PostgreSQL), and graph traversal (Neo4j) to support semantic querying over a large collection of technical documentation. Alongside this, I designed a multimodal RAG pipeline using Jina Embeddings V4 and OpenAI CLIP that enabled natural-language querying over figures and tables.

\vspace{1em}

Before Nokia, I spent two and a half years as a Data Scientist in Maruti Suzuki's R\&D division. I built and deployed an LSTM-based battery health prediction system on vehicle telematics data, achieving 98% field-validated accuracy across more than 100,000 connected vehicles. The system reduced roadside failures and warranty claims at scale, and the underlying method was granted a patent (No.~202411040338). I also audited a training pipeline that was consuming $4,000 per month in GPU compute, identified the bottlenecks, and migrated the workloads to multi-core CPU execution with no loss in model accuracy.

\vspace{1em}

Outside of industry work, I co-authored a paper in \textit{Nature Scientific Reports} on the application of machine learning to high-dimensional genomic data for stress biomarker identification in aquaculture, and I hold a granted patent for the battery prediction system deployed in production across Maruti Suzuki's connected vehicle fleet.

\vspace{1em}

I would love to have an opportunity to work at {{.Company}}. The chance to apply machine learning in this domain is exciting. I look forward to discussing how my background aligns with what your team is building.

\vspace{1.5em}

